.TH CTBREC-DISK-MODE-REMOTE 1 "2026-11-10" "ctbrec-disk-mode-remote" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ctbrec-disk-mode-remote \- manage ctbrec low-disk allowlist mode in the LXC
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ctbrec-disk-mode-remote
\fICOMMAND\fR
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ctbrec-disk-mode-remote
is a local wrapper around
.BR ctbrec-disk-mode (1),
which runs inside the ctbrec LXC (VMID 109) on the Proxmox node. It uploads
the engine and configuration, installs the systemd service and timer, and
exposes status, manual run, reset, log, and uninstall operations from the
workstation.
.P
The local files
.I ~/.local/bin/ctbrec-disk-mode
and
.I ~/.local/bin/ctbrec-disk-mode.json
are the source of truth. The
.B install
command copies them to
.I /usr/local/bin/ctbrec-disk-mode
and
.I /etc/ctbrec-disk-mode.json
in the container.
.P
All container access uses
.BR ssh (1)
with
.B RemoteCommand
disabled, no TTY, and batch mode, followed by
.BR pct (1)
on the Proxmox host.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B install [\-\-keep\-config]
Deploy the engine, configuration, and systemd units, enable and start the
timer, and set ctbrec's native reserve to the configured hard floor. With
.B \-\-keep\-config
an existing remote configuration is left untouched.
.TP
.B status
Show free space, thresholds, mode, allowlist matches, timer state, and the
next scheduled run.
.TP
.B run [\-\-dry\-run]
Evaluate the thresholds once, immediately. With
.B \-\-dry\-run
only print the intended suspend or resume actions.
.TP
.B reset [\-\-dry\-run]
Force the mode off and resume the models it suspended, regardless of free
space. Useful before maintenance or before a manual cleanup.
.TP
.B logs [\-\-lines \fIN\fR]
Show recent service log lines from the journal. Default: 80 lines.
.TP
.B config
Print the remote configuration file.
.TP
.B allowlist
List the local allowlist, one model name per line.
.TP
.BI "allowlist add " "NAME..."
Add one or more model names to the allowlist and deploy the updated
configuration to the container. Names are matched case\-insensitively and
duplicate entries are ignored. If the mode is active, a model that this tool
had suspended is resumed within one timer interval.
.TP
.BI "allowlist remove " "NAME..."
Remove one or more model names from the allowlist and deploy the updated
configuration. Removing a name that is not present is not an error. The last
remaining entry cannot be removed, because the engine requires a non\-empty
allowlist.
.TP
.B uninstall [\-\-purge] [\-\-no\-reset]
Leave the mode (unless
.BR \-\-no\-reset ),
disable and remove the timer and service. With
.B \-\-purge
also remove the remote engine, configuration, and state directory.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CTBREC_DISK_MODE_SERVER
SSH host or alias of the Proxmox node. Default:
.IR proxmox .
.TP
.B CTBREC_DISK_MODE_VMID
LXC ID. Default:
.IR 109 .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/bin/ctbrec-disk-mode
Engine source, deployed to the container.
.TP
.I ~/.local/bin/ctbrec-disk-mode.json
Configuration source, deployed to
.IR /etc/ctbrec-disk-mode.json .
.SH EXAMPLES
Install and start the timer:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-disk-mode-remote install
.EE
.P
Check the current decision:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-disk-mode-remote status
.EE
.P
Preview what a low-disk entry would suspend:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-disk-mode-remote run \-\-dry\-run
.EE
.P
Leave the mode now:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-disk-mode-remote reset
.EE
.P
Add two models to the allowlist and deploy the change:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-disk-mode-remote allowlist add jadetorres_ KamiKiss
.EE
.P
Remove a model from the allowlist:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-disk-mode-remote allowlist remove MilkMeSoftly
.EE
.P
Remove everything, including the deployed engine and config:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-disk-mode-remote uninstall \-\-purge
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
The wrapper exits with the status of the remote command. Bad local options or
a missing engine/config file exit with status 1.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ctbrec-disk-mode (1),
.BR ctbrec-merge (1),
.BR ssh (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written for local use.
